				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1267048&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1608045326" alt="Ihp" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1267048)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/ihp" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1267048); return false;" >Ihp</a></span> <span class="odate time_1439005271 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">08 Aug 2015 03:41</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-2353682">
									

<p>Well, at least it's not another Slashfic. But it still earns a downvote for several reasons:</p>
<ul>
<li>Referring to <em>that bloody list</em> as canon in any context whatsoever. I downvoted the instant I saw that, honestly.</li>
<li>Outright calling Rights a &quot;Team Mom&quot;, complete with Camel Caps. If I want to read TV Tropes, I'll read TV Tropes.</li>
<li>Italicized dialog. What reason is there for the dialog to be italicized?</li>
<li>Even if the dialog wasn't italicized, it feels completely unnatural.</li>
<li>The prose is overwrought.</li>
</ul>
<p>And finally, the most damning reason:</p>
<p>It makes Dr. Rights look like an absolutely horrible person. Now, I'm not a fan of the character by any stretch of the imagination- she's portrayed as such a nymphomaniac that she makes Fanny Hill look chaste- but honestly, the fact that Dr. Rights has a daughter in-universe<sup class="footnoteref"><a id="footnoteref-366658-1" href="javascript:;" class="footnoteref" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnote-366658-1')">1</a></sup> honestly made me wish that she was explored more beyond being &quot;Girl woh fux SPCs lulz&quot;.</p>
<p>Ophelia doesn't seem to have anything wrong with her; Dr. Rights just doesn't love her Because. More specifically, Because we want the reader to feel sad about the fact that this mother doesn't love her daughter. Why? I dunno! Because depression!</p>
<p>This whole &quot;series&quot; has been about Special Snowflake reinterpretations of characters who, let's face it, were already Special Snowflakes before the term was even widely used. And honestly, I am fucking sick of it. If you want to write interpretations of Senior Staff avatars, fine. Go ahead. I may hate the characters, but I can't stop you. At least give them some <span style="text-decoration: underline;">DEPTH</span> beyond being horrible, depressed, sad people, because god knows I get enough of that from myself on any given day.</p>
<p>Downvoted. Fuck this tale.</p>
<div class="footnotes-footer">
<div class="title">Footnotes</div>
<div class="footnote-footer" id="footnote-366658-1"><a href="javascript:;" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.utils.scrollToReference('footnoteref-366658-1')">1</a>. Which, if I am to understand correctly, is based on the fact that yellowdrakex, her writer, had a child herself.</div>
</div>

