			<div class="content" id="post-content-2353800">
									

<p>Hmm.</p>
<p>This is definitely not without fault - I agree with Ihpkmn that the brief dialog sounds nothing like what a person would say (which is a bit of a feat when it stretches over two sentences) and while I'm not quite as angry at the implication the list is canon, the implication in this case had to be rammed in with a maul. Also, the second inclusion of Team Mom (Taking up her mantle as) is irritating and somewhat breaks tone. The first one however is fine, as I find it perfectly plausible Rights would be semi-seriously called Team Mom by a bunch of people who presumably aren't immune to popular culture.</p>
<p>That said, ultimately I rather like it - something about Rights' described constant second-guessing of her own feelings and perceived inability to feel anything for her own daughter, at least as compared with some imaginary version of what she should feel like kinda resonates with me.</p>
<p>So, perhaps a little reluctant +1</p>

